  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance to displaced households of Kabasha, Beni Territory, affected by armed violence.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the rebel group Mai Mai commenced its attack on villages in locations South-West of Beni in late 2013 (such as burning of houses, looting, theft, abductions, torture and rape), communities have been forced to move to nearby locations such as Mataba in Kabasha for safety. Despite the severe vulnerability of these IDPs and host families, they have not received any humanitarian assistance to date. Difficulty to survive has forced some to take risks to return to harvest their fields or return but rebels continue their attacks. 
 
Local partner, SOCOAC has found that priority needs are food security, essential household items, protection and healthcare. This project will provide emergency food and NFI assistance to 606 households/3,030 people (432 displaced and 174 host families) in the locality of Kabasha whose level of vulnerability in food security and NFI is high.  This presentation will focus on &quot;closed fair approach&quot; to give recipients the chance to make their own choices on items they really need.</narrative>
  </description>
